# CollabBoard — Coding Standards & Conventions

Builds on `tdd-workflow`. Follow these when writing or editing code.

## Naming Conventions

| Kind | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| React components | PascalCase | `BoardPage.tsx`, `TopBar.tsx` |
| Functions / variables | camelCase | `subscribeObjects`, `boardId` |
| Types / interfaces | PascalCase | `BoardObject`, `AppUser` |
| Constants | UPPER_SNAKE | `HEARTBEAT_MS`, `REFETCH_DEBOUNCE_MS` |
| Test files | `*.test.ts` / `*.test.tsx` | `presence.test.ts`, `TopBar.test.tsx` |

## Error Handling

- **Do not swallow errors.** Log and rethrow or handle explicitly.
- Use `cancelled` or `abort` flags in async effects to avoid state updates after unmount.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
.catch(() => {})

// ✅ GOOD
.catch((err) => {
  console.error('subscribeObjects error', err)
  return
})
// or for propagating:
throw new DataFetchError('Unable to retrieve board', { cause: err })
```

- In `useEffect` cleanup, set `cancelled = true` before async work completes to avoid stale updates.

## Architecture

- **Feature-based folders:** `auth/`, `board/`, `canvas/`, `ai/`, `supabase/`
- **Types:** Shared types live in `src/types/` (e.g. `board.ts`, `user.ts`)
- **Colocated tests:** Next to source — `Bar.tsx` → `Bar.test.tsx`
- **One concern per module:** Avoid god files; split by responsibility

## Stack Usage

| Use | Avoid |
|-----|----|
| React functional components + hooks | Class components |
| `react-konva` for canvas | Raw canvas or PixiJS (Pre-Search trade-off) |
| Supabase for DB sync (Firestore/RTDB per docs) | Custom WebSockets for sync |
| Vitest + Testing Library | Jest |
| Tailwind for UI | Inline styles except when necessary (e.g. Konva) |
| TypeScript strict mode | `any` without justification |

## Workflow

- **TDD:** See `tdd-workflow` — tests first, then implementation.
- **Commits:** Small, focused commits. Message format: `feat: add X` / `fix: Y` / `test: Z`.
- **PRs:** Must include tests for new behaviour; `npm test` green before merge.

## Non-Negotiables

- Mock external I/O in tests (Supabase, APIs, `window`)
- Keep rules and docs under ~50 lines; prefer actionable examples
